
==============================================================================
SECTION 0 -- base certificates (symbolic identities in QQ[x,y,z])
==============================================================================
[PROVED] E_x(x; F(x,y,z)) == 0 identically              (x-core certificate)
[PROVED] P_r(b-y; F(x,y,z)) == 0 identically            (r-core certificate)
[PROVED] Q_z(z; F(x,y,z)) == 0 identically              (z-core certificate)
[PROVED] disc_X E_x = -4 S^2 L
[PROVED] disc_R P_r = -2916 a^2 L = -4 (27a)^2 L
[PROVED] disc_W Q_z = -4 L M^2,  M/27 = sqrt((729*a**3*b**3*c**4 + 4374*a**3*b**2*c**3 + 8748*a**3*b*c**2 + 5832*a**3*c - 729*a**2*b**4*c**3 - 2754*a**2*b**3*c**2 - 2268*a**2*b**2*c + 648*a**2*b + 27*a*b**6*c**3 + 297*a*b**5*c**2 + 360*a*b**4*c - 268*a*b**3 - 9*b**7*c**2 - 28*b**6*c + 28*b**5)**2)
         => all three coordinate cubics obey disc = -4 (square)^2 L  (level-1 law)
[PROVED] det J_F = -2
[PROVED] L irreducible over QQ

==============================================================================
SECTION 1 -- certified fiber section Y(x), Z(x) and the norm objects
==============================================================================
r(x) = 3*a*x*(9*a*c*x - b*x + 2)/(12*a*x**2 - b**2*x**2 + b*x + 2)
[PROVED] F(x, Y(x), Z(x)) == (a,b,c) mod E_x(x): the generic middle fiber is
         the graph w |-> (w, Y(w), Z(w)) over the roots of E_x (off x=0, Yden=0)
[PROVED] L(x,Y,Z) = Mnum(x)/(x^4 Yden(x)^4),  deg_x Mnum = 13

==============================================================================
SECTION 2 -- TASK 1: the second-level Jelonek factor L_2 (exact)
==============================================================================
pseudo-reduction: L^11 * Mnum = Q*E + Rm,  deg_x Rm = 2
N := Res_x(E, Rm) exact; 14719 terms  [t=60s]
[PROVED] G := Res_x(E, Yden) = 8 a^2 S^2  (the level-1 disc square factor S
         returns as the section-collision norm)
exact factorization: N = L^22 * c^4 * G^4 * (kappa * L_2)
kappa = 1/4   (so Res_x(E,Rm) = kappa L^22 c^4 G^4 L_2 exactly)
L_2: primitive integer polynomial; total degree 25; degrees (a,b,c)=(14,21,12);
     361 terms; lex-leading term 3^21 * a^14 * c^11
[PROVED] L_2 irreducible over QQ:
   content_a(L_2) = 1 (no a-free factor) and the exact slice L_2(a,5,7) keeps
   full degree 14 and is QQ-irreducible; a factorization L_2 = G*H with
   deg_a G, deg_a H >= 1 would slice nontrivially.  Over C: closure(F(Z(L)))
   is irreducible and Q-defined, so its equation is a Q-rational irreducible
   factor of L_2 = L_2 itself.
forward points  s in Z(L) -> t=F(s):  [asserting L(s)=0 and L_2(t)=0]
   s=(-1/4, 1, 20/27): L_2(F(s)) = 0
   s=(2/3, 3, 1/3): L_2(F(s)) = 0
   s=(-7/4, 2, 16/49): L_2(F(s)) = 0
   s=(-2, 5, -3): L_2(F(s)) = 0
   s=(-11/4, 4, 24/121): L_2(F(s)) = 0
   s=(5/432, 1/2, 56/25): L_2(F(s)) = 0
   family point s=(0,2,1/2) -> t=(33/2,2,0): L_2(t)=0, L(t)=260 != 0
   family point s=(1,4,0) -> t=(1280,772,-10): L_2(t)=0, L(t)=-23184 != 0
   3 generic off-points have L != 0 and L_2 != 0  [OK]
[PROVED] closure(F(Z(L))) = Z(L_2):
  (i)   wherever a generic fiber point lies on Z(L), the certified section makes
        Mnum vanish at a root of E, so N(t)=0: F(Z(L))~ lies in
        Z(N) = Z(L) u Z(c) u Z(a) u Z(S) u Z(L_2);
  (ii)  F(Z(L))~ is irreducible of dim 2 (Z(L) irreducible; F finite-to-one by
        the THM-2546 fiber law), hence inside ONE component;
  (iii) at t = F(1,4,0) = (1280,772,-10): L,a,c,S all nonzero, L_2(t)=0;
        so the component is Z(L_2), and dimensions force equality.
NORM LAW [PROVED by root-product identities + the exact factorization of N]:
     prod_{s in F^{-1}(t)} L(s)  =  L_2(t) / (64 L(t))                    (*)
   (prod Mnum(w_i) = Res(E,Rm)/L^35;  prod w_i^4 = 16c^4/L^4;
    prod Yden(w_i)^4 = G^4/L^8;  Res(E,Rm) = kappa L^22 c^4 G^4 L_2, kappa=1/4.)
   50-digit numeric cross-check of (*) at t=(2, 5, 7)  [OK]
   50-digit numeric cross-check of (*) at t=(1, 1, 1)  [OK]
(L_2 pickled to 05-knowledge/results/keller_L2_polynomial_opus_20260728.pkl)

==============================================================================
SECTION 3 -- TASK 1b: S_{FoF} = Z(L) u Z(L_2)  (exact spot verification)
==============================================================================
Containment [standard: properness composes]:
   S_{FoF} subseteq S_F u F(S_F) = Z(L) u Z(L_2)      (THM-2473 + Section 2).
S_{FoF} is closed of pure codim 1 (Jelonek), so each component equals Z(L) or
Z(L_2); membership is settled by one exact fiber-drop witness per component
(etale + count < 9 => non-proper: the THM-2473 (3) argument).  Level-1 counts
use the PROVED THM-2546 law: 3 off Z(L); 1 on Z(L), T!=0; 0 on L=T=0.
   t1=(Fraction(-1, 4), Fraction(1, 1), Fraction(20, 27)) on Z(L)\Z(L_2): middle fiber = the survivor q_s=(Fraction(5, 6), Fraction(-3, 2), Fraction(7, 1)),
      L(q_s)=25529/24 != 0  =>  #fiber(FoF)(t1) = 3 < 9      [DROP on Z(L)]
   t2 on Z(L_2)\Z(L): t=(Fraction(1280, 1), Fraction(772, 1), Fraction(-10, 1)): r=1 middle points on Z(L) (T=0 among them: 0) => #fiber = 7
      the on-L middle point is q=(1,4,0): L(q)=0, T(q)=4 => inner fiber 1;
      7 = 3+3+1 exactly                                  [DROP on Z(L_2)]
   t3 off both:       t=(Fraction(1, 1), Fraction(1, 1), Fraction(1, 1)): r=0 middle points on Z(L) (T=0 among them: 0) => #fiber = 9
   t4=(Fraction(4, 27), Fraction(4, 3), Fraction(1, 1)) on {L=T=0}: level-1 fiber EMPTY => #fiber(FoF)=0 (omitted curve persists)
[VERDICT Task 1] TOWER PREDICTION CONFIRMED:
   S_{FoF} = Z(L) u Z(L_2), with exact drop pattern 3 / 7 / 9 / 0 at the four
   witnesses.  L_2 is PROVED exact (irreducible, deg 25, box (14,21,12),
   361 terms) and prod_fiber L = L_2/(64 L).

==============================================================================
SECTION 4 -- TASK 2: disc tower on the degree-9 x-eliminant of F o F
==============================================================================
Per-slice construction (exact over QQ):
   E9(xi; a) = primitive_a,xi part of Res_w( E_x(w; a,b0,c0), Chat(xi,w) ),
   Chat = (w^4 Yden^4) * E_x(xi; q(w)),  q(w) = (w, Y(w), Z(w)).
Its 9 roots are the x-coordinates of the FoF fiber (product over the middle
fiber of the inner x-cores).
--- slice (b,c) = (5, 7) ---
   deg_xi = 9; xi^8 coefficient == 0 (trace-zero depressed structure persists)
   lead_xi(E9) = (-1) * L_2|slice   [x-lead IS the level-2 Jelonek factor]
   multiplicity of L_2 in disc: 1 (ODD);  multiplicity of L: 8 (EVEN)
   sqf(disc * L_2|slice): factor multiplicities [(2, 85), (8, 2)] -> ALL EVEN: True (const class 17179869184)
   sqf(disc * L * L_2 |slice): the ONLY odd factor is L|slice (mult [9])
--- slice (b,c) = (2, 3) ---
   deg_xi = 9; xi^8 coefficient == 0 (trace-zero depressed structure persists)
   lead_xi(E9) = (-1) * L_2|slice   [x-lead IS the level-2 Jelonek factor]
   multiplicity of L_2 in disc: 1 (ODD);  multiplicity of L: 8 (EVEN)
   sqf(disc * L_2|slice): factor multiplicities [(2, 85), (8, 2)] -> ALL EVEN: True (const class 274877906944)
   sqf(disc * L * L_2 |slice): the ONLY odd factor is L|slice (mult [9])
--- slice (b,c) = (-1, 2) ---
   deg_xi = 9; xi^8 coefficient == 0 (trace-zero depressed structure persists)
   lead_xi(E9) = (-1/4) * L_2|slice   [x-lead IS the level-2 Jelonek factor]
   multiplicity of L_2 in disc: 1 (ODD);  multiplicity of L: 8 (EVEN)
   sqf(disc * L_2|slice): factor multiplicities [(2, 85), (8, 2)] -> ALL EVEN: True (const class 1099511627776)
   sqf(disc * L * L_2 |slice): the ONLY odd factor is L|slice (mult [9])
[VERDICT Task 2] Prediction "odd part of disc = L * L_2 (each odd)" is
HALF-REFUTED: on all three independent exact slices
     disc_xi(E9) = c0 * (H * L^4)^2 * L_2
so the odd part is L_2 ALONE; L enters to EVEN order 8.  Function-field
mechanism (pieces proved above; disc(fg)=disc f disc g Res(f,g)^2):
     prod_i disc(E_i) = (-4)^3 NS^2 * NL == -NL == -L_2/L      (mod squares, by (*))
     [prod_{i<j} Res(E_i,E_j)]^2 == -L                          (mod squares: the
         cross-resultant is antisymmetric in the middle roots, so its square
         carries the middle-cubic discriminant class -4S^2L == -L)
     product: (-L_2/L)(-L) = L_2  (mod squares).
The middle level's -L class cancels against the norm's 1/L: a conductor-
discriminant mechanism.  Level-k expectation (NOT asserted): odd part = L_k alone.

