   L_W2 = L o T^{-1}  (target covariance CONFIRMED);
   disc_X E = -4 (S o tau)^2 L_W2;  disc_R P = -2916 (a o tau)^2 L_W2;
   disc_W Q = -4 (M o tau)^2 L_W2          [the -(det J)^2 = -4 law, all cores]
   leads {L_W2, -2, 8} = {L, -|detJ|, |detJ|^3}  [lead pattern CONFIRMED]
   W1: 3 random exact fiber points annihilated by the pulled-back x-core [OK]
   W2: 3 random exact fiber points annihilated by the pulled-back x-core [OK]
[VERDICT Task 3] PROVED for BOTH members (W2 is explicit in THM-2465):
   disc = -4 (square)^2 * L_W for each of the three coordinate cores, with
